// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CMSIS field macros
//
// In an SDK build PERI_TINGPU.h already declares the mask, the shift and the
// functional form of every field, so these are for the standalone side only.
// The offset table carries a mask and a shift per field but no functional
// form, so the mask and the shift are taken from the table through TINGPU_REG,
// the same macro the register offsets above use, and the TINGPU_<REG>_<FLD>(x)
// builder the table lacks is stated here, spelled as PERI_TINGPU.h spells it.
//
// Only fields whose CMSIS counterpart holds the same value are listed. A
// field of an array register is stated once under the array base name, as
// PERI_TINGPU.h does, so S2_SCISSOR_CTRL0_MINX and its siblings all map
// to TINGPU_S2_SCISSOR_CTRL_MINX.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

